 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Blurred Images:** The method tolerates up to 10% blurred images, but higher rates may degrade the SIFT matching and Mask R-CNN accuracy [S1].
-*   **Empty Regions:** Poisson reconstruction requires empty rates $\le 5\%$ to ensure geometric continuity; larger gaps may result in incomplete geometry [S1].
-*   **Semantic Accuracy:** The method relies on 92% segmentation accuracy; misclassification of product vs. background may lead to incorrect weight assignment and suboptimal detail preservation [S1].
+*   **Blurred Images:** The method tolerates a fault rate of $\le$10% blurred images, but exceeding this may degrade the COLMAP reconstruction and semantic segmentation accuracy [S1].
+*   **Empty Regions:** Poisson reconstruction is used to handle empty regions, but if the empty rate exceeds 5%, the geometric continuity may be compromised [S1].
+*   **Semantic Accuracy:** The method relies on 92% accurate semantic masks. Misclassification could lead to incorrect weight assignment during optimization [S1].
 
